xmodel/grok-approaches.md:274:**(c) Stuck.** Riemann existence is generous: once you allow enough 2-cycles at infinity, \(S_n\) (or \(A_n\)) fillings exist. Kistner–Shaska’s dim-3 result that geometric monodromy is full \(A_n/S_n\) except at degree 3 is the *opposite* of a kill — it says monodromy is generic. Qiu’s “\(A_{21}\) monodromy excludes (72,108)” is artifact-less and should be ignored (`RECON.md`). The one historically successful dessin attack (Suzuki) is a dressed Bézout certificate on an edge polynomial, i.e. §1 in costume. A global “the monodromy cannot be primitive of degree \(td\)” statement would be §23, and is untried.
